# TASK-260715-15vkvz rework 02 evidence

Implemented a FIFO non-reentrant repository operation gate across ensure, enable, disable, remove, and duplicate repair. Repair convergence calls the internal held-operation implementation so it cannot deadlock or open a second mutation window. Deterministic held-load tests prove each public entry point performs no second load or mutation before the active operation reaches its terminal result; concurrent zero-manager ensure creates and saves exactly one canonical manager.

Both iOS and macOS NetworkExtension seams now decode NSNumber by exact Objective-C integer representation. Boolean and fractional values are rejected as type-confused, Int(1) remains current, Int.max remains a signed future version, and UInt64.max is preserved through an unsigned manager-version/error representation without intValue truncation or overflow. Ensure, enable, disable, remove, and repair tests prove zero mutation for unsupported/type-confused/future values.

