     5	
     6	## 2026-07-21
     7	
     8	### 0442 — Apple VPN terminal observation registers before authoritative status (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
     9	- REGRESSION: Both NetworkExtension adapters read `NEVPNConnection.status` before installing `NEVPNStatusDidChange`, so a terminal transition in that gap could be lost and an already-stopped session could falsely reach the 15-second `stopTimedOut` path.
    10	- FIX: iOS and macOS now install the observer first and then perform an authoritative status read through an injectable seam. The locked retirement handshake also handles a synchronous terminal notification before registration returns its token: completion wins once, and the late-arriving token is immediately unregistered.
    11	- COVERAGE: A deterministic two-platform matrix covers terminal-before-registration, terminal-during-registration without a notification, notification-before-token-return, notification-first completion, duplicate/late notification retirement, and cancellation. Every terminal/cancel path unregisters once and produces at most one completion.
    12	- VERIFICATION: Focused normal and Thread Sanitizer runs each pass 33 tests; `make validate-core` passes 251 tests in 24 suites plus build; strict Swift format, tracked/untracked diff, and board validation are clean; generic iOS Simulator and macOS adapter builds succeed with signing disabled.
    13	
    14	### 0421 — VPN preference operations are non-reentrant and NSNumber versions are exact (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
    15	- REGRESSION: Actor isolation did not serialize repository calls across suspended NetworkExtension callbacks, so concurrent operations could load and mutate overlapping manager generations. Both platform seams also used `NSNumber.intValue`, truncating `1.5` to current version 1 and overflowing `UInt64.max` into repairable corruption.
    16	- FIX: Every public ensure/enable/disable/remove/repair entry point now crosses one FIFO operation gate, held through its terminal result; internal repair convergence reuses the held operation without re-entering the gate. Manager-contract inspection carries signed `Int` or unsigned `UInt64` versions without narrowing, while Boolean, fractional, and other type-confused versions fail closed with zero mutations.
    17	- COVERAGE: Deterministic held-callback tests queue every repository operation and prove no second load or mutation before the first terminal result; concurrent zero-manager ensure creates and saves exactly one canonical manager. Both iOS and macOS seams cover `NSNumber(true)`, `1.5`, `UInt64.max`, `Int.max`, and `Int(1)`, including zero-write ensure/enable/disable/remove/repair paths.
    18	- VERIFICATION: The focused suite and Thread Sanitizer each pass 27 tests. `make validate-core` passes 245 tests in 24 suites plus the post-test build; strict Swift format lint, diff/board checks, and generic iOS Simulator/macOS adapter builds pass. A first parallel platform-build attempt hit SwiftPM's shared build-database lock; the independent sequential macOS rerun succeeded.
    19	
    20	### 0405 — VPN manager rework preserves all future versions and fresh authority (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
    21	- REGRESSION: Future manager-contract versions were narrowed through `UInt16(exactly:)`, so 65,536 and `Int.max` fell into repairable corruption. Explicit enable also returned early when already enabled and could save during connecting, reasserting, or disconnecting.
    22	- FIX: Manager-contract `updateRequired` now carries the original `Int` without narrowing; every version greater than v1 remains unsupported future data. Explicit enable returns `sessionTransitionInProgress` before setters or saves for all three transitions, while an already-enabled manager still performs the user-intent setter/save/fresh-reload verification path.
    23	- FRESHNESS: The preference fake now materializes a distinct manager after every successful save. Stale retries re-evaluate unrelated, unmarked, and `Int.max` future replacements without mutating them, and verification rejects a distinct persisted manager whose canonical fields do not match the requested write.
    24	- VERIFICATION: The focused repository suite passes 23 tests. `make validate-core` passes boundary/native-package checks, 241 tests in 24 suites, and the post-test build; strict Swift format lint, `git diff --check`, and board validation pass. Generic iOS Simulator and macOS adapter builds both succeed.
    25	

